1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,242
MAN:

2
00:00:00,242 --> 00:00:05,500
Sandra – I seem to remember you had some family visitors staying with you recently.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:05,882
SANDRA:

4
00:00:05,882 --> 00:00:06,879
Yeah that’s right.

5
00:00:06,879 --> 00:00:10,190
My brother and his family were here a couple of months ago.

6
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:10,240
MAN:

7
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:11,213
OK good.

8
00:00:11,213 --> 00:00:15,307
Well I wanted to ask your advice – I’ve got my cousin

9
00:00:15,307 --> 00:00:20,764
and her family visiting next month and as I don’t have kids I’ve no

10
00:00:20,764 --> 00:00:22,470
idea where to take them.

11
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:22,774
SANDRA:

12
00:00:22,774 --> 00:00:23,078
Right.

13
00:00:23,078 --> 00:00:23,990
What about accommodation?

14
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:27,030
Are they going to stay with you in your flat?

15
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:27,385
MAN:

16
00:00:27,385 --> 00:00:32,000
No, thankfully – there wouldn’t be room – my cousin wants me to recommend

17
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,710
a hotel.

18
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:34,130
Do you know anywhere?

19
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:34,507
SANDRA:

20
00:00:34,507 --> 00:00:36,016
Yes, I do actually.

21
00:00:36,016 --> 00:00:39,410
I always recommend people stay at the Kings Hotel.

22
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:39,684
MAN:

23
00:00:39,684 --> 00:00:40,780
Where’s that near?

24
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,104
SANDRA:

25
00:00:41,104 --> 00:00:45,316
It’s about five minutes’ walk from Murray Station – so nice and central.

26
00:00:45,316 --> 00:00:47,260
It’s actually on George Street.

27
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:47,607
MAN:

28
00:00:47,607 --> 00:00:48,995
Oh yes I know.

29
00:00:48,995 --> 00:00:53,852
I think they’re on quite a tight budget – so how much roughly is

30
00:00:53,852 --> 00:00:55,240
it to stay there?

31
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:55,597
SANDRA:

32
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:59,885
If you book a family room it’s about £125 per night.

33
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:03,457
My brother paid for two double rooms in the end

34
00:01:03,457 --> 00:01:07,030
and I think that was around £95 for each room.

35
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:07,241
MAN:

36
00:01:07,241 --> 00:01:08,510
Oh that’s not too bad.

37
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:08,804
SANDRA:

38
00:01:08,804 --> 00:01:11,160
So how old are your cousin’s kids?

39
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:11,500
MAN:

40
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,520
Twelve and nine.

41
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:16,260
So I want to organise some trips while they’re here.

42
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:16,564
MAN:

43
00:01:16,564 --> 00:01:20,520
I was thinking of doing a bus tour of the city centre – as

44
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:22,650
none of them have been here before.

45
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:22,956
SANDRA:

46
00:01:22,956 --> 00:01:24,794
Those bus tours are quite expensive.

47
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:29,082
I think it’s better to do a walking tour – it gives you a

48
00:01:29,082 --> 00:01:30,920
much better feel for the city.

49
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,176
SANDRA:

50
00:01:31,176 --> 00:01:33,221
There’s one that starts from Carlton Square.

51
00:01:33,221 --> 00:01:36,290
It takes a couple of hours and doesn’t cost that much.

52
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:36,584
MAN:

53
00:01:36,584 --> 00:01:37,173
Sounds good.

54
00:01:37,173 --> 00:01:38,940
I’ll look that up – thanks.

55
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:39,205
SANDRA:

56
00:01:39,205 --> 00:01:42,918
If the weather’s nice, one thing you could do is visit the old

57
00:01:42,918 --> 00:01:43,183
fort.

58
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:44,774
You can get there by boat.

59
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:46,630
The whole trip takes half a day.

60
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:46,924
MAN:

61
00:01:46,924 --> 00:01:48,685
That’s a really good idea.

62
00:01:48,685 --> 00:01:50,740
I’d like to do that myself.

63
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:51,033
MAN:

64
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:55,431
And if the weather’s bad I was thinking they could go to the Science

65
00:01:55,431 --> 00:01:55,725
Museum.

66
00:01:55,725 --> 00:01:58,950
But maybe they could do that when I’m at work.

67
00:01:58,950 --> 00:01:59,270
SANDRA:

68
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:02,150
Yeah – don’t forget it’s closed on Mondays.

69
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:02,494
MAN:

70
00:02:02,494 --> 00:02:07,306
They’re here from Saturday for four nights – so Tuesday would be best, I

71
00:02:07,306 --> 00:02:07,650
think.

72
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:07,961
SANDRA:

73
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:08,272
Mmm,

74
00:02:08,272 --> 00:02:10,758
and it won’t be so crowded then.

75
00:02:10,758 --> 00:02:11,690
Saturdays are terrible.

76
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:11,943
SANDRA:

77
00:02:11,943 --> 00:02:14,724
I took my kids to the exhibition on old computers there

78
00:02:14,724 --> 00:02:16,241
and it was far too crowded.

79
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:18,770
I wanted to go back but it’s finished now.

80
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:19,081
MAN:

81
00:02:19,081 --> 00:02:20,324
That’s a shame.

82
00:02:20,324 --> 00:02:22,810
My cousin’s kids would have enjoyed that.

83
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:23,109
SANDRA:

84
00:02:23,109 --> 00:02:26,990
There’s another one starting soon on space which looks really good too.

85
00:02:26,990 --> 00:02:27,343
MAN:

86
00:02:27,343 --> 00:02:30,520
OK, well I’ll mention that to my cousin.

87
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:30,800
SANDRA:

88
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,600
Have you thought about where to take them to eat?

89
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:33,928
MAN:

90
00:02:33,928 --> 00:02:37,532
Well I really like all the food stalls at Clacton Market.

91
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:42,447
My cousin’s vegetarian – I know it’s one of the best places for that

92
00:02:42,447 --> 00:02:43,430
kind of food.

93
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:43,733
SANDRA:

94
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:44,036
Definitely,

95
00:02:44,036 --> 00:02:47,370
and there’ll be loads of choice for the kids, too.

96
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:47,641
SANDRA:

97
00:02:47,641 --> 00:02:51,169
You need to get there quite early though – at the weekend most of

98
00:02:51,169 --> 00:02:53,340
the stalls stop serving lunch at 2.30.

99
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:53,666
MAN:

100
00:02:53,666 --> 00:02:54,319
Good point.

101
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:56,929
It’s all going to need careful planning!

102
00:02:56,929 --> 00:03:02,149
My cousin said she’d love to take the kids to a show at the theatre –

103
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:03,780
but tickets are so expensive!

104
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,134
SANDRA:

105
00:03:04,134 --> 00:03:04,841
I know.

106
00:03:04,841 --> 00:03:10,148
But you can get some good deals if you book online with bargaintickets.com for

107
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:14,040
the following day – on some seats there’s a 75% discount.

108
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:14,400
MAN:

109
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:14,760
Really?!

110
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,920
I must try and get some.

111
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:17,180
SANDRA:

112
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:17,439
Yeah.

113
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:20,812
There are lots of things you can do for free as well – no

114
00:03:20,812 --> 00:03:22,110
need to spend a fortune.

115
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:22,503
MAN:

116
00:03:22,503 --> 00:03:23,290
Like what?

117
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:23,622
SANDRA:

118
00:03:23,622 --> 00:03:25,617
They’re coming next month, right?

119
00:03:25,617 --> 00:03:30,603
Well, check and see if it’s the same weekend as the Roots Music Festival

120
00:03:30,603 --> 00:03:31,600
in Blakewell Gardens.

121
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,577
MAN:

122
00:03:32,577 --> 00:03:34,530
R double-O-T-S?

123
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:34,836
SANDRA:

124
00:03:34,836 --> 00:03:35,141
Yeah.

125
00:03:35,141 --> 00:03:36,363
Check it out online.

126
00:03:36,363 --> 00:03:40,030
It’s always a family-friendly event and there’s no entry charge.

127
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:40,395
MAN:

128
00:03:40,395 --> 00:03:41,490
That sounds perfect.

129
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:41,789
SANDRA:

130
00:03:41,789 --> 00:03:45,976
And if you’re in Blakewell Gardens – climb Telegraph Hill – you’ll be able

131
00:03:45,976 --> 00:03:48,069
to look right down on the port.

132
00:03:48,069 --> 00:03:51,060
Everyone’s always really impressed because it’s so huge.

133
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:51,350
MAN:

134
00:03:51,350 --> 00:03:54,540
Oh yeah – I’ve been meaning to do that for ages.

135
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,570
I’ve heard the view’s amazing.

136
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:56,841
SANDRA:

137
00:03:56,841 --> 00:03:57,112
Yeah.

138
00:03:57,112 --> 00:03:58,740
It’s really worth the effort.

139
00:03:58,740 --> 00:03:59,248
MAN:

140
00:03:59,248 --> 00:04:03,315
Well that’s given me loads of ideas.

141
00:04:03,315 --> 00:04:04,840
Thanks so much …
